  "experiment_id": "2026-09-24-e27-prefill-interval",
  "title": "E27: native prefill cadence (--prefill-schedule-interval 8) on the E22b recipe",
  "outcome": "promote",
  "outcome_detail": "Owner accepted. Running agents decode 2.9-5.4x faster while another request cold-prefills 8-32K tokens; against the same-day control, C4 per-stream TTFT +35.1% and C4 -3.3%, code decode -1.85% and prose -2.25% (unresolved: all three candidate code-decode suites are below both controls, but load and order effects are not separated), C1 +3.3%, code TTFT +3.5% and C1 per-stream TTFT +3.0%; prefill and replay within about 2%.",
  "reference": {
    "baseline_id": "2026-09-23-e22b",
    "baseline_sha256": "7454e85cb1b1ac6ad4a04f4f88bca19b98955d238f0c4b315bf28aace31866bd"
  },
  "coverage": "Three complete native suites (162 requests) on one retained load, the interference phase on the same load, then two same-day E22b control suites (108 requests) after one transition back.",
  "client_transport": "Direct LAN HTTP to the rank-0 API for the candidate and the same-day control; the frozen E22b reference used an SSH tunnel over a direct Tailscale path. Compare against the same-day control for effects smaller than a few percent.",
